<p>Port Arthur roof damage insurance claims tend to turn on a few questions: Was the damage caused by a covered storm? Can the roof be repaired, or does it need replacement? And what will the policy actually pay once deductibles, depreciation, and roof endorsements are applied? Those questions get more complicated in Jefferson County, where many roofs are insured through TWIA and every re-roof needs both a city permit and TDI windstorm inspection. This page walks through what typically matters on a roof claim here.</p>

<h2>Common Roof Types and Damage in Port Arthur</h2>
<p>Most homes around Port Arthur have composition shingle roofs. Older neighborhoods include many roofs that have been replaced more than once, sometimes with layers or mixed materials. Commercial and industrial properties near the refineries and the port often have metal roofs or low-slope membrane systems.</p>
<table>
